# Host wording differs (gcc: implicit declaration; clang: call to undeclared): pin the part both print.
# A commented prototype declares nothing, so the lowerer sees no
# declaration of 'ghost'; the receiver is a double with no method set,
# so the call is emitted as ghost(u) and the host refuses it, at this
# line: a compile error, not a link error.
ufcs_bare_comment_decl_fail.ccs:8:
function 'ghost'
